# Local field-test failure memory

At the start of work on this project, check whether `.local-agent-memory/failure_cases.md` exists.
If it exists, **read it** before implementation decisions involving:

- voice interaction / turn-taking / open-mic
- navigation (embedded Amap or guidance speech)
- realtime conversation behavior (Baidu Flex end-to-end)
- field testing, device QA, or bug fixing from real-world reports

## How to treat statuses

- `OPEN` and `INVESTIGATING` = **active known problems**
- Do **not** claim `FIXED` only because code changed
- `FIXED` only after an appropriate **automated** test succeeds
- `VERIFIED` only after **real-device / field** evidence is recorded in that case
- Prefer updating an existing case over creating a duplicate when a new report matches

## When the owner reports a new real-world failure in chat

Add it to `.local-agent-memory/failure_cases.md` unless they explicitly say not to.
That directory is **gitignored** — never commit or push it; never put secrets, coordinates, or full transcripts into tracked docs as a substitute.
